## Coverage and approval boundary

The 6,700/22,071-byte archived requests, 10,305/27,370 input bounds and 16 headline items per request match the supplied evidence. The 64 available entry counts and possible 80-item current projection have static-source plus authenticated historical-input support; current packet composition and zero-rejection omission have no claimed dynamic execution. Historical six-call/448,000-token capabilities and reservation arithmetic support only the described archived-request comparison. They provide neither a future packet bound nor renewed spending authority.

Lifecycle attempts, evaluated rounds and rejection records remain distinct. Two failed historical archives do not satisfy the future requirement for two distinct evaluated rounds with critic, checkpoint and successful cleanup evidence. The listed rejection, duplicate, positive-metric, finalization, absence/error and novelty branches remain unexecuted where stated. No production three-universe, held-out qualification, replay or promotion validity follows from this provisional SP500 development evidence.

C-c may now prepare a distinct campaign/root, exact manifest/config and initial outbound packets with hashes/sizes, coherent finite call/token and lifecycle reserves, affordable rejection handling, fixed environment/deadline/cleanup authority, explicit stop conditions and one saved launch. It must then obtain the fresh separate user execution grant required by section 12. Historical remaining budget is not replacement-run authorization.

No tests, synthetic cases, archive authentication or summary reruns, provider/API/Docker calls, environment/credential reads, campaigns, operational Git actions, source edits or subagents were used. Only this review document was written.

